# Count Palindromic Subsequences —

```java
/*
Problem:
Given a string s made of lowercase English letters, count the number of
distinct palindromic subsequences of length 3. A valid subsequence is of the form:
x _ x  (first and last characters same, middle can vary)
We must count unique subsequences, not total occurrences.

Example:
Input:  "aabca"
Distinct palindromic subsequences:
"aba", "aaa", "aca"
Output: 3

Approach:
1. Track the first and last occurrence of each character (a–z).
2. For each character c:
     - Look between first[c] and last[c]
     - Count unique characters in between → these form palindromes c _ c
3. Sum across all 26 letters.

Time Complexity:  O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1) aside from minimal arrays and a small set.
*/

class Solution {
    public int countPalindromicSubsequence(String s) {
        int[] first = new int[26];
        Arrays.fill(first, -1);
        int[] last = new int[26];
        int n = s.length();

        // Record first & last occurrence
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int ind = s.charAt(i) - 'a';
            if (first[ind] == -1) {
                first[ind] = i;
            }
            last[ind] = i;
        }

        int ans = 0;

        // For each letter as the outer character
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            if (first[i] == -1) continue;

            Set<Character> set = new HashSet<>();
            for (int j = first[i] + 1; j < last[i]; j++) {
                set.add(s.charAt(j));
            }
            ans += set.size();
        }

        return ans;
    }
}
